WEBVTT

00:13.750 --> 00:15.708
- Hey!
- Yeah!

00:17.250 --> 00:18.583
There you go.

00:27.500 --> 00:30.415
I had a friend
Was a big baseball player

00:30.416 --> 00:33.124
Hey. Hey, whoa, hey. Who gave you this?

00:33.125 --> 00:34.124
Grandpa.

00:34.125 --> 00:36.291
Yeah? I gotta keep an eye on you.

00:36.958 --> 00:38.166
I love you, pal.

00:39.291 --> 00:40.665
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:40.666 --> 00:41.707
Happy Fourth.

00:41.708 --> 00:43.832
- You remember Hayden.
- Hey, good to see you again.

00:43.833 --> 00:46.749
- Likewise. Good to see you.
- Hey. Welcome. We got lots of food.

00:46.750 --> 00:47.707
Okay.

00:47.708 --> 00:50.082
There he is.

00:50.083 --> 00:52.082
I wanted you to meet my friend Hayden.

00:52.083 --> 00:53.500
Hey, buddy.

00:54.083 --> 00:57.208
Your Aunt Rachel tells me that
you already know how to do a high five.

00:58.041 --> 00:59.957
Up high. All right.

00:59.958 --> 01:01.165
You're late.

01:01.166 --> 01:02.165
I brought wine.

01:02.166 --> 01:04.125
- Oh, then you're forgiven.
- Thank you.

01:05.625 --> 01:07.165
So you two back together?

01:07.166 --> 01:09.249
No. Just friends.

01:09.250 --> 01:10.333
Mm-hmm.

01:12.250 --> 01:13.915
- Hey.
- I need to go potty.

01:13.916 --> 01:16.166
Oh, then we need to go potty.

01:20.166 --> 01:21.166
Hey, Hayden.

01:22.125 --> 01:23.083
Thank you.

01:23.791 --> 01:27.249
- Did you give Matthew a sparkler?
- I did. It's the Fourth of July.

01:27.250 --> 01:29.041
Let a three-year-old play with fire?

01:30.416 --> 01:32.958
It's a sparkler, David.
It's not a blowtorch.

01:40.041 --> 01:42.500
Who's the guy with the, uh,
interesting hair?

01:44.666 --> 01:46.207
That's Kyle Bergin.

01:46.208 --> 01:49.499
Dave and I went to high school with him.
Everyone called him Skunk.

01:49.500 --> 01:52.332
Must have been a long four years,
nickname like that.

01:52.333 --> 01:54.749
He loved the name. Skunk.

01:54.750 --> 01:57.083
It's like he wanted to work
for Nicky Fisher from the jump.

02:05.708 --> 02:07.582
Everything okay?

02:07.583 --> 02:08.750
It's fine.

02:30.708 --> 02:32.041
Hold still.

02:35.666 --> 02:39.457
If Hilde's willing to go on the record
and admit she lied on the stand,

02:39.458 --> 02:42.749
we'd have enough to go to the police
and get a new trial.

02:42.750 --> 02:44.666
I don't want a new trial.

02:45.625 --> 02:47.125
I just want my son back.

02:52.833 --> 02:55.166
All right, well,
let's go raid Hayden's closet

02:55.833 --> 02:57.333
and find Hilde Winslow.

03:01.416 --> 03:03.665
What if Hilde doesn't show
to get her mail?

03:03.666 --> 03:05.500
We gonna stand at Postal Works forever?

03:06.333 --> 03:09.749
Jim wasn't able to get her address,
but maybe Adam could.

03:09.750 --> 03:11.165
He's law enforcement, right?

03:11.166 --> 03:15.040
Adam and Philip risked everything for me.
I'm not gonna ask them for more help.

03:15.041 --> 03:16.166
I get it.

03:17.000 --> 03:20.999
Well, I rent a PO box near my house.
I'm assuming Hilde does the same thing.

03:21.000 --> 03:23.957
So we know her general neighborhood.

03:23.958 --> 03:26.124
We could go there,
you keep an eye on Postal Works,

03:26.125 --> 03:29.415
and I could cruise around,
see if she's out and about.

03:29.416 --> 03:30.583
Might get lucky.

03:31.791 --> 03:34.582
Were your sister and David close
when you two were married?

03:34.583 --> 03:38.124
Uh, well, David and I met
our first year at Amherst,

03:38.125 --> 03:41.208
so I guess Rachel has known him
as long as I have.

03:41.833 --> 03:44.125
And when was the last time you two spoke?

03:44.916 --> 03:46.374
Last week.

03:46.375 --> 03:49.165
Uh, she's helping me
plan my baby shower, so…

03:49.166 --> 03:51.624
Did you know she was at Briggs
visiting your ex-husband

03:51.625 --> 03:52.915
the day before he escaped?

03:52.916 --> 03:53.750
No.

03:54.458 --> 03:58.040
Any reason why your ex-husband
might be headed to New York?

03:58.041 --> 04:01.375
No. Is that where you think he's going?

04:03.583 --> 04:07.374
If your sister contacts you,
you need to call us immediately.

04:07.375 --> 04:08.791
I can show you out.

04:19.166 --> 04:21.624
Please let us know
if there's anything we can do to help.

04:21.625 --> 04:23.583
Thank you.

04:25.625 --> 04:28.457
You just lied to the FBI.
Do you know how serious that is?

04:28.458 --> 04:29.915
We don't know what happened.

04:29.916 --> 04:32.207
She called you from Maine
the day before he escaped.

04:32.208 --> 04:34.540
You don't think the FBI,
they can check your phone records?

04:34.541 --> 04:37.249
- What am I supposed to do?
- Tell them the truth.

04:37.250 --> 04:40.124
- She is my sister.
- I understand that, I do.

04:40.125 --> 04:42.750
But your sister…
She's gonna land you in jail.

04:44.750 --> 04:46.416
I need to get ready for this fundraiser.

05:00.375 --> 05:01.749
Sarah. Hey.

05:01.750 --> 05:05.249
So I was hoping you would
put in a good word for me with Max.

05:05.250 --> 05:07.790
- About what?
- To partner up when you leave.

05:07.791 --> 05:09.249
How do you know about that?

05:09.250 --> 05:12.249
I got a buddy in the Seattle office.
Wait, you haven't told him yet?

05:12.250 --> 05:14.249
We're kind of in the middle
of a manhunt here.

05:14.250 --> 05:16.790
Okay, well, it'd be a shame if he found
out before you had a chance to tell him.

05:16.791 --> 05:19.540
Of course, I'd be happy to do you a favor.
Keep it to myself.

05:19.541 --> 05:20.833
Subtle.

05:23.500 --> 05:25.790
- Undercover team's in place?
- Since last night.

05:25.791 --> 05:28.499
And I pulled in tac agents
from Brooklyn to expand our coverage.

05:28.500 --> 05:29.582
Mobile command?

05:29.583 --> 05:31.957
A surveillance van in an alley
around the corner from Hilde.

05:31.958 --> 05:33.958
DOT is standing by for traffic.

05:39.625 --> 05:41.207
News said he took you hostage.

05:41.208 --> 05:42.125
No.

05:43.125 --> 05:45.875
Adam and I broke him out.
It was the only way to protect him.

05:46.541 --> 05:47.541
Protect him from what?

05:48.416 --> 05:51.624
Rachel Mills came to visit David.

05:51.625 --> 05:54.915
She showed him a photo of a little boy
around 8 years old.

05:54.916 --> 05:57.290
It was taken at an amusement park
a few weeks ago.

05:57.291 --> 05:59.874
David believes the boy
in the photo is Matthew.

05:59.875 --> 06:01.166
What?

06:03.041 --> 06:05.374
We buried him, Philip. You were there.

06:05.375 --> 06:07.290
Right after David saw the photo,

06:07.291 --> 06:10.207
there were back-to-back attempts
made on his life.

06:10.208 --> 06:12.207
I do not think they were a coincidence.

06:12.208 --> 06:14.332
I think they happened
because David saw that photo.

06:14.333 --> 06:17.415
What if we were wrong
about what happened that night?

06:17.416 --> 06:18.916
Everything pointed to him.

06:20.583 --> 06:22.000
Not everything.

06:24.291 --> 06:26.457
- What is he talking about, Lenny?
- Nothing.

06:26.458 --> 06:29.499
Don't you dare do that. Not about this.

06:29.500 --> 06:31.916
Hilde Winslow lied on the stand.

06:32.750 --> 06:35.082
David didn't bury the bat
in the woods that night.

06:35.083 --> 06:37.208
How could you possibly know that?

06:37.833 --> 06:38.875
Because we did.

06:43.250 --> 06:44.915
The night of the murder,

06:44.916 --> 06:48.083
the responding officers,
they realized who David was.

06:49.416 --> 06:50.500
They called me.

06:53.250 --> 06:55.458
I was on scene before the detectives.

06:56.666 --> 06:57.750
I found the bat.

06:58.958 --> 07:02.165
I knew David would never
consciously hurt Matthew.

07:02.166 --> 07:04.165
It had to be a night terror.

07:04.166 --> 07:06.791
I-I-I panicked. I called Philip.

07:07.375 --> 07:09.500
And we buried it.

07:12.375 --> 07:15.999
I thought maybe without a murder weapon,

07:16.000 --> 07:17.291
he'd get off.

07:18.541 --> 07:20.750
We have to tell someone.

07:21.375 --> 07:24.999
Tell them what, Soph?
The murder weapon was inside the house?

07:25.000 --> 07:26.916
It makes him even more guilty.

07:28.000 --> 07:29.375
What we did,

07:29.958 --> 07:32.625
we did because
we thought David had done it.

07:33.666 --> 07:35.332
But if Matthew is still alive,

07:35.333 --> 07:40.125
that means someone else is behind
everything that happened that night.

07:41.833 --> 07:43.500
And they're still out there.

08:09.750 --> 08:10.916
Hey, it's me.

08:12.458 --> 08:13.833
We need to talk.

08:17.333 --> 08:18.833
- Thanks so much.
- Enjoy.

08:26.875 --> 08:28.290
- Hey.
- Hey.

08:28.291 --> 08:31.125
David's escape is all over the news.
Where are you?

08:31.916 --> 08:33.000
I'm in New York.

08:33.500 --> 08:35.874
You're going after Hilde Winslow,
aren't you?

08:35.875 --> 08:36.832
Jim…

08:36.833 --> 08:39.207
I know that you're looking
for a way back in.

08:39.208 --> 08:42.874
If half of what you've told me is true,
and David really is innocent,

08:42.875 --> 08:45.874
this is the story of a lifetime.

08:45.875 --> 08:49.874
All right, well, this isn't about a story.
This is about finding Matthew.

08:49.875 --> 08:51.375
Why can't it be both?

08:53.500 --> 08:55.041
Listen, I gotta go.

09:05.375 --> 09:06.749
No sign of Hilde?

09:06.750 --> 09:08.291
- No. You?
- No.

09:09.250 --> 09:11.540
Walked every street
within a three-block radius

09:11.541 --> 09:15.416
until the siren call
of cheese and sauce diverted me.

09:20.541 --> 09:21.832
Wow.

09:21.833 --> 09:23.624
It's good. I forgot how good that is.

09:23.625 --> 09:25.958
See? If you would've allowed visitors,

09:26.750 --> 09:29.083
I could've snuck you in
a slice from Sal's.

09:30.541 --> 09:31.708
Why didn't you?

09:32.750 --> 09:35.083
I guess I felt like I wanted to disappear.

09:36.625 --> 09:37.791
I get that.

09:43.250 --> 09:45.124
We only need her address
from the mail, right?

09:45.125 --> 09:47.499
Yeah, which is inside the PO box.

09:47.500 --> 09:50.165
You said you rent a box in Revere,
so you got a key?

09:50.166 --> 09:51.915
- Why?
- Just give it to me.

09:51.916 --> 09:53.416
Here. What's her number?

09:53.958 --> 09:55.832
- Forty-two.
- Okay.

09:55.833 --> 09:58.457
You… You gonna tell me your plan?

09:58.458 --> 09:59.666
Where's the fun in that?

10:18.875 --> 10:20.540
Goddamn it.

10:20.541 --> 10:21.707
Excuse me.

10:21.708 --> 10:23.208
What can I do for you?

10:23.750 --> 10:27.124
I'm trying to get the mail for my mom,
and the key broke.

10:27.125 --> 10:28.500
It's stuck in the lock.

10:29.166 --> 10:30.790
It's been one of those weeks.

10:30.791 --> 10:32.790
You wouldn't happen to have
a master key or something

10:32.791 --> 10:34.332
that you can get it from other side?

10:34.333 --> 10:36.125
Her name's Harriet Winchester.

10:47.791 --> 10:49.625
- Nice to see you.
- Nice to see you.

10:54.541 --> 10:57.666
- I just have to take this. Okay? Sorry.
- Of course, yeah.

11:00.500 --> 11:01.416
Hello?

11:02.041 --> 11:02.958
Hi.

11:03.458 --> 11:05.125
Oh my God, Rachel.

11:05.750 --> 11:08.416
What's going on?
I've been trying to call you.

11:09.000 --> 11:10.250
I know. I'm sorry.

11:10.916 --> 11:12.874
Please tell me you're not with David.

11:12.875 --> 11:13.833
I am.

11:14.458 --> 11:16.041
But I can explain why.

11:18.208 --> 11:20.540
Oh my God. I, uh…

11:20.541 --> 11:22.415
I shouldn't be talking to you.

11:22.416 --> 11:23.957
Can I just tell you why?

11:23.958 --> 11:26.332
No. I don't care, okay?

11:26.333 --> 11:29.624
I don't care why you did it
or what you're doing in New York.

11:29.625 --> 11:31.415
Wait, how do you know we're in New York?

11:31.416 --> 11:33.499
Because an FBI agent
was at my house this morning

11:33.500 --> 11:36.750
telling me if I heard from you,
I had to call them.

11:37.458 --> 11:40.290
Give me one reason
why I shouldn't turn you both in.

11:40.291 --> 11:41.458
It's about Matthew.

11:44.375 --> 11:45.708
We think he's alive.

11:49.208 --> 11:50.208
Cheryl?

11:52.458 --> 11:53.999
Why would you say that to me?

11:54.000 --> 11:56.166
It's the truth, okay? I…

11:56.916 --> 11:58.499
It's why I'm helping David.

11:58.500 --> 11:59.666
Stop it.

12:01.291 --> 12:03.541
We think he's alive, Cheryl.

12:05.416 --> 12:07.125
We think Matthew's alive.

12:25.875 --> 12:27.416
Are you okay, dear?

12:30.750 --> 12:32.166
Yeah.

12:44.000 --> 12:44.875
Here you go.

12:47.875 --> 12:49.000
Thank you.

12:50.583 --> 12:52.207
Is everything all right?

12:52.208 --> 12:53.541
Just hormones.

12:55.583 --> 12:58.208
I'm Gertrude, by the way. It's a pleasure.

12:59.791 --> 13:02.250
Ahem, uh, Cheryl Dreason.

13:04.208 --> 13:05.499
Dr. Dreason, actually.

13:05.500 --> 13:09.999
This is my fundraiser, and here I am
falling apart in the ladies' room.

13:10.000 --> 13:13.582
Nonsense. Pregnancy can be
quite the emotional roller coaster,

13:13.583 --> 13:14.957
if memory serves.

13:14.958 --> 13:17.832
It's been a tough day,

13:17.833 --> 13:22.458
and… now I have to go
and deliver this huge speech.

13:23.208 --> 13:27.207
Sorry. I don't usually open up
to strangers in the bathroom.

13:27.208 --> 13:29.958
Well, then it's a good thing
we're no longer strangers, isn't it?

13:31.458 --> 13:33.291
Keep it. I always carry a spare.

13:34.083 --> 13:35.375
You're too kind.

13:35.958 --> 13:39.458
Good luck. Something tells me
you're going to do just great.

13:53.791 --> 13:54.999
Harriet Winchester,

13:55.000 --> 13:58.708
a.k.a. Hilde Winslow,
18 Mercer Court, Apartment 3B.

13:59.500 --> 14:01.416
The FBI knows we're in New York, David.

14:02.291 --> 14:03.500
How?

14:04.166 --> 14:05.332
Just talked to Cheryl.

14:05.333 --> 14:07.708
They were at her house,
asking why you might be here.

14:09.000 --> 14:10.207
It's Matthew's file.

14:10.208 --> 14:11.957
I circled Hilde's name in my notes.

14:11.958 --> 14:14.332
They must have found it
and put it together.

14:14.333 --> 14:16.291
They'll be waiting for us.

14:32.875 --> 14:33.875
Mackenzie.

14:34.541 --> 14:35.708
Burroughs.

14:36.375 --> 14:38.791
- It's been a while.
- They finally made you sergeant, huh?

14:39.875 --> 14:42.458
- How are you holding up, Lenny?
- What's going on, Murph?

14:42.958 --> 14:43.791
Why are we here?

14:44.708 --> 14:47.041
We got a call this morning
about a desecration.

14:52.250 --> 14:53.125
What the hell?

14:53.750 --> 14:55.750
Lenny, maybe you should let me do this.

15:07.458 --> 15:10.083
Jesus Christ. Who did this?

15:13.125 --> 15:15.124
- Who did this?
- We don't know yet.

15:15.125 --> 15:18.915
Yeah? Well, that's my grandson's
empty coffin at the bottom of a dirt hole.

15:18.916 --> 15:21.082
- So you might want to get on it.
- Okay.

15:21.083 --> 15:22.582
What do you know, Murph?

15:22.583 --> 15:24.665
Some guy on the maintenance crew
said he saw a truck

15:24.666 --> 15:26.499
leaving the grounds early this morning.

15:26.500 --> 15:28.290
A black Toyota Tundra.

15:28.291 --> 15:31.499
Had some damage on the left back bumper.
We'll find him, Lenny.

15:31.500 --> 15:32.916
Yeah, hey, Murph, uh…

15:33.875 --> 15:34.790
thanks a lot.

15:34.791 --> 15:36.208
Yeah, you bet.

15:38.958 --> 15:40.375
What if it was David?

15:41.333 --> 15:43.125
What if he came back here?

15:44.791 --> 15:46.333
I don't think it was.

15:59.416 --> 16:00.291
Perimeter check.

16:01.208 --> 16:02.041
No sign.

16:03.000 --> 16:04.875
No sign.

16:06.791 --> 16:10.458
Businesswoman has been pretending
to hail a cab for a half hour now.

16:11.041 --> 16:13.499
And not to be critical
of our civil service workers,

16:13.500 --> 16:17.124
but local mailman has been organizing
his bag since we got here.

16:17.125 --> 16:18.540
How am I gonna get in?

16:18.541 --> 16:19.750
Afraid you're not.

16:20.791 --> 16:22.207
We need a plan B.

16:22.208 --> 16:24.458
There isn't one. Hilde's the only lead.

16:25.041 --> 16:26.749
Maybe there's a service entrance out back.

16:26.750 --> 16:28.165
That's gonna be covered.

16:28.166 --> 16:31.416
We could try to draw her out.
Call in a bomb threat or something.

16:32.750 --> 16:34.290
Okay, what if I go in? Right?

16:34.291 --> 16:36.332
I can ask her all the same questions.

16:36.333 --> 16:38.832
I mean, you're the fugitive, right?
Not me.

16:38.833 --> 16:40.791
We've got to assume they're after you too.

16:41.625 --> 16:42.791
Good point.

16:50.375 --> 16:51.624
Take my burner.

16:51.625 --> 16:53.000
I've got an idea.

16:53.708 --> 16:54.957
Chopra, you good?

16:54.958 --> 16:58.332
I am. You can count on me
as the last line of defense, boss.

16:58.333 --> 16:59.375
Hmm.

17:01.500 --> 17:04.457
Hey, I need to talk to you
about something later.

17:04.458 --> 17:06.332
Well, let me guess.

17:06.333 --> 17:10.333
Julie wasn't in your office yesterday
to talk about a TikTok video.

17:11.500 --> 17:13.540
Do you ever get tired
of knowing everything?

17:13.541 --> 17:14.375
No.

17:17.875 --> 17:20.083
Holy shit. Is that Rachel Mills?

17:20.958 --> 17:22.500
- Where?
- Right there.

17:23.666 --> 17:24.666
I'll be damned.

17:25.250 --> 17:29.208
Anybody seeing Burroughs?
Come on, people, anybody seeing him?

17:31.583 --> 17:34.707
Be advised, Rachel Mills
is approaching the building.

17:34.708 --> 17:36.708
Alpha team, move in and take her.

17:38.833 --> 17:39.666
FBI!

17:40.458 --> 17:41.457
Stop right there.

17:41.458 --> 17:43.790
Show us your hands, now!

17:43.791 --> 17:45.041
Whoa, whoa.

17:45.541 --> 17:48.291
Turn around, put your hands on your head.
Interlock your fingers.

17:49.125 --> 17:50.375
Okay, okay! Hey, hey, hey.

18:06.000 --> 18:09.083
This is Bravo 2.
Rachel Mills is in custody.

18:09.708 --> 18:12.583
- Is everything all right?
- Yes, ma'am. Just step back inside.

18:16.333 --> 18:18.083
- Don't shoot!
- Step back inside.

18:19.041 --> 18:20.041
Over there.

18:22.166 --> 18:23.333
All right.

18:30.291 --> 18:33.290
Stop! Stop! Sit down! Sit down!

18:33.291 --> 18:35.957
- Please don't hurt me.
- At my trial, you lied on the stand.

18:35.958 --> 18:38.707
No, you did it.
I saw you bury the bat in the woods.

18:38.708 --> 18:41.083
I've got nothing to lose,
so if you keep lying, I'll kill you.

18:43.250 --> 18:44.541
Ms. Mills.

18:45.583 --> 18:47.416
I'm Agent Williams. This is Agent Greer.

18:48.208 --> 18:50.540
So, you want to tell us
where David Burroughs is?

18:50.541 --> 18:51.915
How would I know that?

18:51.916 --> 18:53.624
We pulled your cell phone records.

18:53.625 --> 18:56.457
We know he called you
right after he escaped.

18:56.458 --> 18:59.457
Which is when
you left the diner to go pick him up.

18:59.458 --> 19:01.375
Who told you to lie?

19:02.041 --> 19:03.457
Who has my son?

19:03.458 --> 19:04.874
What are you talking about?

19:04.875 --> 19:05.958
They took him.

19:07.375 --> 19:09.916
The people that told you to lie.

19:11.000 --> 19:14.415
That's-- That's not possible.
They-- They told me you did it.

19:14.416 --> 19:16.458
That you were gonna get away with it.

19:17.041 --> 19:18.125
Who told you?

19:19.583 --> 19:21.082
I can't. They'll kill me.

19:21.083 --> 19:22.832
Here's how this is gonna work.

19:22.833 --> 19:25.665
You will tell us everything you know,

19:25.666 --> 19:29.124
and if you prove useful
in helping us capture David,

19:29.125 --> 19:32.874
we might consider making a deal
to reduce your charges.

19:32.875 --> 19:36.749
- Which include accessory to murder.
- What?

19:36.750 --> 19:40.290
You drove David to Officer Ted Wesson's
home, where he executed him.

19:40.291 --> 19:45.500
Rachel, that is a life sentence,
so you need to think before you answer.

19:47.166 --> 19:48.541
Give me their names.

20:02.083 --> 20:04.916
That's your daughter, right?
She was a schoolteacher? I remember.

20:06.375 --> 20:07.583
That's Elle.

20:09.000 --> 20:11.665
A parent would do anything
to keep their child safe.

20:11.666 --> 20:13.916
And I couldn't protect Matthew that night.

20:14.625 --> 20:16.375
That's why I'm doing all this.

20:17.416 --> 20:18.499
That's just it.

20:18.500 --> 20:21.666
That's why I lied. To protect her.

20:22.666 --> 20:24.291
Elle had a gambling problem.

20:24.916 --> 20:27.124
One day, a man shows up at my door.

20:27.125 --> 20:29.332
He tells me
that you beat your son to death

20:29.333 --> 20:32.749
and that if I help put you away,
they'll forgive her debt.

20:32.750 --> 20:33.583
What man?

20:34.166 --> 20:35.499
He didn't tell me his name,

20:35.500 --> 20:38.957
but he had jet-black hair
with a white forelock running through it.

20:38.958 --> 20:40.250
Skunk.

20:42.375 --> 20:45.500
He said I didn't have a choice.
He told me who he worked for.

20:46.541 --> 20:47.833
Nicky Fisher.

20:50.500 --> 20:52.665
Where is David?

20:52.666 --> 20:54.165
I honestly don't know.

20:54.166 --> 20:56.749
You don't? Yeah, okay. Enjoy prison.

20:56.750 --> 20:57.625
Come on.

20:59.625 --> 21:02.624
Okay. Okay, fine.
I came here to talk to Hilde Winslow.

21:02.625 --> 21:03.625
What about?

21:04.541 --> 21:05.707
She lied on the stand.

21:05.708 --> 21:07.082
Why would she lie?

21:07.083 --> 21:09.915
I don't know,
but she changed her name after the trial.

21:09.916 --> 21:12.540
She sold her house,
and she basically disappeared.

21:12.541 --> 21:13.957
That doesn't strike you as odd?

21:13.958 --> 21:15.958
So she moved. So what?

21:16.458 --> 21:17.749
So, what if David's innocent?

21:17.750 --> 21:20.082
That's why they build prisons.
They're all innocent.

21:20.083 --> 21:22.415
If you really came here
to talk to Hilde Winslow,

21:22.416 --> 21:24.083
then why'd you wait so long to tell us?

21:25.458 --> 21:26.458
Hmm?

21:34.583 --> 21:36.083
Because she's stalling.

21:38.958 --> 21:40.375
Burroughs is inside.

21:41.250 --> 21:43.832
All units, Burroughs is inside
the apartment.

21:43.833 --> 21:45.500
Third floor, unit B, move in.

21:48.000 --> 21:49.291
Shit.

21:50.708 --> 21:52.874
I'm sorry I lied. Let me help you.

21:52.875 --> 21:55.040
There's a fire escape
out my bedroom window.

21:55.041 --> 21:57.000
It-- It'll take you to the street.

22:09.708 --> 22:10.916
Burroughs, freeze!

22:16.958 --> 22:18.500
He-- He went out the bedroom window.

22:22.500 --> 22:24.374
He's on the roof.

22:24.375 --> 22:26.790
Get me a bird in the air.
Lock down these streets.

22:26.791 --> 22:28.375
Agent Greer is in pursuit.

22:36.541 --> 22:37.666
Stop!

22:56.125 --> 22:57.208
Ah!

23:01.625 --> 23:02.458
Stop!

23:54.208 --> 23:57.458
David Burroughs, put your hands up now!

23:58.666 --> 24:01.249
Hands up and get off of the ledge!

24:01.250 --> 24:02.416
I can't go back.

24:07.625 --> 24:09.541
No! No! Oh, shit!

24:23.875 --> 24:27.666
Suspect last seen on Mercer.
Requesting backup to canvas the area.

24:39.250 --> 24:40.957
It's Hilde Winslow.

24:40.958 --> 24:44.290
David Burroughs was just in my apartment
asking questions about his son.

24:44.291 --> 24:45.832
Did the cops get him?

24:45.833 --> 24:47.708
No. No, he escaped.

24:48.541 --> 24:51.499
What if he comes back?
What am I supposed to do?

24:51.500 --> 24:54.125
You just keep your mouth shut.

24:55.625 --> 24:57.083
I'm on my way.

25:29.958 --> 25:30.791
Adam?

25:35.833 --> 25:36.833
Adam?

25:38.458 --> 25:39.666
Dad?

25:43.208 --> 25:44.416
Lenny?

25:47.541 --> 25:48.624
What's wrong?

25:48.625 --> 25:51.208
You really gonna stand there
and pretend like you don't know?

25:52.750 --> 25:54.999
You dug up Matthew's grave.
You took his body.

25:55.000 --> 25:57.375
No. That's not what happened.

25:59.791 --> 26:01.458
Then tell us what did.

26:02.708 --> 26:06.332
Yes, I went to the cemetery
and I dug up the coffin.

26:06.333 --> 26:07.540
Why?

26:07.541 --> 26:09.583
Because I wanted
to test the DNA of the body.

26:11.166 --> 26:14.375
Prove that it wasn't Matthew,
that David was telling the truth.

26:16.375 --> 26:18.083
Only there wasn't a body.

26:19.583 --> 26:21.957
What are you talking about?
How could there be no body?

26:21.958 --> 26:23.999
Because I wasn't
the first one to dig it up.

26:24.000 --> 26:26.375
Somebody opened it
with a crowbar a long time ago.

26:26.958 --> 26:28.999
And there's only one reason to do that.

26:29.000 --> 26:31.207
They knew the boy
who was buried wasn't Matthew,

26:31.208 --> 26:33.250
and they wanted to make sure
no one ever found out.

26:35.375 --> 26:36.375
Hang on.

26:37.916 --> 26:39.583
- Hey. You okay?
- I'm fine.

26:50.875 --> 26:53.957
- Where did you get that?
- I pulled it from the precinct.

26:53.958 --> 26:55.208
After I got suspended.

26:56.875 --> 26:58.833
Adam, I'm sorry.

26:59.500 --> 27:00.625
It's okay.

27:02.333 --> 27:04.249
We gotta look at everything again.

27:04.250 --> 27:06.499
There's gotta be something
that they missed.

27:06.500 --> 27:09.541
Something that could point us
to who set David up and took Matthew.

27:11.125 --> 27:12.540
With your generosity,

27:12.541 --> 27:16.832
we can ensure that every child
has access to the best possible care,

27:16.833 --> 27:19.832
giving families
in their most desperate hour

27:19.833 --> 27:21.166
what they truly need.

27:22.166 --> 27:23.333
Hope.

27:29.208 --> 27:30.708
Oh, thank you.

27:31.416 --> 27:33.540
- Dr. Dreason.
- Dr. Heller.

27:33.541 --> 27:35.499
- Wonderful speech.
- Thank you.

27:35.500 --> 27:36.457
How are you feeling?

27:36.458 --> 27:37.582
Ah, pregnant.

27:37.583 --> 27:40.165
Oh, would you excuse me a second?

27:40.166 --> 27:41.666
- Of course.
- Thank you.

27:42.708 --> 27:44.916
- You were fantastic.
- Thank you.

27:46.500 --> 27:48.916
I'd like to introduce you
to Gertrude Payne.

27:49.916 --> 27:52.250
Gertrude Payne of the Payne Foundation.

27:52.833 --> 27:54.583
It was a lovely speech.

27:55.125 --> 27:56.040
Thank you.

27:56.041 --> 27:57.624
When I found out
Ms. Payne was in attendance,

27:57.625 --> 27:59.374
I knew that you two needed to meet.

27:59.375 --> 28:01.291
- We've met, actually.
- Oh.

28:02.000 --> 28:04.915
Your foundation does
so much for this city.

28:04.916 --> 28:08.415
We are honored to have you here.
If I'd have known--

28:08.416 --> 28:10.541
I try to fly under the radar
whenever I can.

28:11.791 --> 28:14.207
You know my father
started the Payne Foundation

28:14.208 --> 28:15.874
after the Second World War.

28:15.875 --> 28:19.999
He very much wanted to serve,
but his physical detected a heart murmur.

28:20.000 --> 28:23.290
And then it was later revealed
that my grandfather,

28:23.291 --> 28:25.874
who had amassed
quite a fortune by that point,

28:25.875 --> 28:29.540
had paid to have his records altered
to keep him from the front lines.

28:29.541 --> 28:32.665
Can't blame a parent
for wanting to protect their child.

28:32.666 --> 28:34.457
Well, that's a very kind way
of putting it.

28:34.458 --> 28:37.749
My father always wondered what happened
to that young man who took his place,

28:37.750 --> 28:40.291
knowing that he probably
never made it home.

28:40.958 --> 28:43.208
And so he wanted to repay his debt.

28:43.833 --> 28:47.958
And to use the privilege
that had spared his life to help others.

28:48.625 --> 28:50.708
Balance the scales, so to speak.

28:52.416 --> 28:56.916
I cannot think of anyone
who I would trust more in that endeavor.

28:57.958 --> 29:00.749
Expect a substantial donation
from our foundation

29:00.750 --> 29:02.458
to help you meet your goals.

29:03.666 --> 29:06.416
Wow, I… I don't know what to say.

29:07.791 --> 29:09.666
- Well, we accept.
- Oh! Yeah.

29:10.833 --> 29:13.375
Well, it was a pleasure
meeting you, Dr. Dreason.

29:14.000 --> 29:14.916
Twice.

29:16.583 --> 29:19.166
So, wait. When did you two meet?

29:19.750 --> 29:21.000
In the bathroom.

29:21.625 --> 29:24.416
Embarrassing, but I was really upset.

29:25.625 --> 29:27.708
That call you took earlier
was from Rachel, wasn't it?

29:28.583 --> 29:29.416
Yeah.

29:30.916 --> 29:32.833
What did she say? Is she with David?

29:35.541 --> 29:37.458
Did she say why she's doing this?

29:40.416 --> 29:41.416
No.

29:42.958 --> 29:44.416
We need to call the FBI.

29:45.500 --> 29:48.083
I know. I just-- I need more time.

29:50.333 --> 29:51.375
Please.

30:08.333 --> 30:09.582
How'd it go?

30:09.583 --> 30:12.000
She got a phone call during the luncheon.

30:12.500 --> 30:14.457
I think it was from her sister.

30:14.458 --> 30:16.333
Do you think she'll be an issue?

30:16.916 --> 30:18.790
Well, a new husband, a baby on the way,

30:18.791 --> 30:21.750
and now a fully funded program
to help keep her occupied?

30:22.958 --> 30:26.458
No, I don't think she'll be a problem.

30:27.750 --> 30:29.041
That's good.

30:29.791 --> 30:31.166
What about Burroughs?

30:33.625 --> 30:37.249
He broke into Hilde Winslow's apartment,
and then he proceeded to escape again.

30:37.250 --> 30:41.291
How many government agencies
does it take to arrest this man?

30:42.875 --> 30:44.540
Is he still in New York?

30:44.541 --> 30:47.291
I'm working on it.
But there's more bad news.

30:48.000 --> 30:50.749
Rachel Mills was detained by the FBI.

30:50.750 --> 30:52.125
She has the photo.

30:54.875 --> 30:56.457
In more breaking news,

30:56.458 --> 30:59.540
shots were fired
in Manhattan earlier this afternoon

30:59.541 --> 31:03.874
after eyewitnesses reported seeing a man
pursued by police in Midtown

31:03.875 --> 31:05.207
at an apartment building.

31:05.208 --> 31:07.915
And we are now learning
the identity of that man.

31:07.916 --> 31:10.082
His name, David Burroughs.

31:10.083 --> 31:13.666
A convicted murderer who escaped
from a maximum security prison…

31:15.083 --> 31:16.458
Hayden.

31:18.833 --> 31:20.583
Where the hell is Rachel?

31:24.541 --> 31:28.082
Rachel Mills, you're under arrest
for aiding and abetting David Burroughs

31:28.083 --> 31:30.666
as well as an accessory
in the murder of Ted Wesson.

31:39.291 --> 31:40.749
Yeah, just about a block that way.

31:40.750 --> 31:42.582
- Hey.
- Hey.

31:42.583 --> 31:43.416
You all right?

31:44.125 --> 31:45.832
Yeah. Don't I look okay?

31:45.833 --> 31:49.124
Don't be a wiseass, Sarah. What were
you thinking, jumping across that roof?

31:49.125 --> 31:51.416
I was thinking about getting Burroughs.

31:52.083 --> 31:54.208
- I had him.
- Agent Greer, we're heading out.

31:55.125 --> 31:56.375
Would you just…

32:03.041 --> 32:05.707
Can you just be careful? Okay?

32:05.708 --> 32:06.708
Please?

32:07.416 --> 32:08.832
Can you do that?

32:08.833 --> 32:11.333
This isn't your boss
talking to you either.

32:13.041 --> 32:16.040
Listen, I don't ever want to have to make
that phone call to your mother.

32:16.041 --> 32:17.041
Understand?

32:17.625 --> 32:19.666
She already hates me as it is.

32:21.000 --> 32:22.750
I'm careful, Dad.

32:23.958 --> 32:25.125
I gotta go.

32:28.125 --> 32:29.208
Let's go.

32:55.916 --> 32:56.958
Theo!

32:58.291 --> 33:00.458
Come on! It's time for dinner!

33:01.708 --> 33:03.041
Be right there!
